    "description": "### Impact\r\nAuthenticated users could exploit unescaped SQL LIKE wildcards in upload lookups to resolve uploads they cannot access and disclose restricted metadata such as original filenames and secure-upload paths. This fix escapes LIKE metacharacters in all upload-resolution patterns, restoring literal identifier matching so wildcard input no longer selects unrelated upload records across the metadata, URL-lookup, and cooked-video-placeholder paths.\r\n\r\n### Patches\r\nUpgrade to the patched version.\r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\nUpgrade to the patched version.",
